WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.544 --> 00:00:19.605
"My favorite Thanksgiving food is cranberry sauce," Izzie said.

2
00:00:19.606 --> 00:00:22.816
It was the day before Thanksgiving vacation.

3
00:00:22.817 --> 00:00:25.768
Everyone was excited about the holiday.

4
00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:28.922
"I like sweet potatoes," Ethan said.

5
00:00:28.923 --> 00:00:32.761
"Where's Bobby?" Miss Shelly asked.

6
00:00:32.762 --> 00:00:34.465
Ethan shrugged.

7
00:00:34.466 --> 00:00:36.726
"His mom picked him up early today.

8
00:00:36.727 --> 00:00:39.741
I think he had a doctor's appointment."

9
00:00:39.742 --> 00:00:42.448
"Oh," Miss Shelly said.

10
00:00:42.449 --> 00:00:47.108
"I didn't get to wish him a Happy Thanksgiving."

11
00:00:47.109 --> 00:00:49.813
"Did someone say Thanksgiving?"

12
00:00:49.814 --> 00:00:52.340
Bobby hurried into the gym.

13
00:00:52.341 --> 00:00:55.985
He was carrying a plastic container and a basketball.

14
00:00:55.986 --> 00:00:59.854
"Ethan said you left school early," Izzie said.

15
00:00:59.855 --> 00:01:02.724
"I did," Bobby said.

16
00:01:02.725 --> 00:01:06.117
"But I didn't want to miss Kids Central today.

17
00:01:06.118 --> 00:01:10.084
It's the last one before Thanksgiving vacation."

18
00:01:10.085 --> 00:01:14.348
Jason stared at him. "You look different."

19
00:01:14.349 --> 00:01:19.076
Bobby grinned and started dribbling the basketball across the gym.

20
00:01:19.077 --> 00:01:21.269
He jumped up.

21
00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:25.202
Whoosh! The ball sailed through the hoop.

22
00:01:25.203 --> 00:01:30.336
Nina laughed. "I know what's different!"

23
00:01:30.337 --> 00:01:32.941
"Me too!" Izzie said.

24
00:01:32.942 --> 00:01:38.963
"You got your cast off, Bobby!"

25
00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:43.138
"Congratulations," Miss Shelly said.

26
00:01:43.139 --> 00:01:47.543
"Thanks." Bobby picked up the plastic container.

27
00:01:47.544 --> 00:01:50.401
"I made something to thank you guys."

28
00:01:50.402 --> 00:01:54.689
"Huh?" Jason said. "What did we do?"

29
00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:59.298
"You made having a broken leg more fun," Bobby said.

30
00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:02.052
"We did?" Izzie asked.

31
00:02:02.053 --> 00:02:03.601
Bobby nodded.

32
00:02:03.602 --> 00:02:06.805
"Missing soccer season was terrible.

33
00:02:06.806 --> 00:02:10.047
But you guys helped me and we had fun."

34
00:02:10.048 --> 00:02:12.699
He opened the container.

35
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.980
"See? Thanksgiving cookies.

36
00:02:15.981 --> 00:02:19.280
They're shaped like turkeys, but don't worry.

37
00:02:19.281 --> 00:02:21.855
They taste like chocolate."

38
00:02:21.856 --> 00:02:25.078
"They look delicious," Miss Shelly said.

39
00:02:25.079 --> 00:02:29.637
"They'll go great with our activity today."

40
00:02:29.638 --> 00:02:32.542
"What are we making?" Jason asked.

41
00:02:32.543 --> 00:02:35.985
"Thankful pumpkin pies," Miss Shelly said.

42
00:02:35.986 --> 00:02:41.058
"Don't you mean Thanksgiving pumpkin pies?" Izzie asked.

43
00:02:41.059 --> 00:02:42.567
"Nope."

44
00:02:42.568 --> 00:02:47.437
Miss Shelly had a stack of paper plates, paint, markers, and pots of glitter.

45
00:02:47.438 --> 00:02:50.156
The kids gathered around the table.

46
00:02:50.157 --> 00:02:53.954
"These pies aren't for eating," Miss Shelly explained.

47
00:02:53.955 --> 00:02:57.871
"They're a fun way to share what you're thankful for."

48
00:02:57.872 --> 00:03:02.067
"Oh, I get it." Nina read from the board.

49
00:03:02.068 --> 00:03:08.647
"Step one: Paint the inside circle of a paper plate orange.

50
00:03:08.648 --> 00:03:11.702
That's for the pie filling.

51
00:03:11.703 --> 00:03:16.813
Then paint the outside edge tan for the piecrust."

52
00:03:16.814 --> 00:03:21.821
"Step two: Stick three cotton balls to the paint."

53
00:03:21.822 --> 00:03:24.537
Bobby laughed.

54
00:03:24.538 --> 00:03:29.498
"Cool! That will look like whipped cream on top of the pumpkin filling."

55
00:03:29.499 --> 00:03:36.501
"Step three: Sprinkle with glitter to look like spices and sugar," Ethan said.

56
00:03:36.502 --> 00:03:39.122
Everyone painted their plates.

57
00:03:39.123 --> 00:03:46.642
"Let's have Bobby's cookies while the paint dries," Miss Shelly said.

58
00:03:46.643 --> 00:03:51.286
Soon Izzie ran to the pies. "The paint's dry!"

59
00:03:51.287 --> 00:03:53.723
Nina looked at the board.

60
00:03:53.724 --> 00:04:00.287
"Step five: use letter stickers to spell, 'I'm Thankful For . . .'

61
00:04:00.288 --> 00:04:06.483
And then cut out a slice of pie with scissors."

62
00:04:06.484 --> 00:04:09.241
"Step six," Jason read.

63
00:04:09.242 --> 00:04:12.583
"Write five things you're thankful for."

64
00:04:12.584 --> 00:04:18.276
"Easy," Ethan said. "I'm thankful for Bobby's cookies!"

65
00:04:18.277 --> 00:04:22.759
After everyone wrote their five things, Nina read the next step.

66
00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:26.526
"Put the painted plate on top of the white plate.

67
00:04:26.527 --> 00:04:30.795
Connect them loosely with a brass paper fastener."

68
00:04:30.796 --> 00:04:34.545
"Now spin!" Izzie said.

69
00:04:34.546 --> 00:04:38.021
Everyone spun their plates.

70
00:04:38.022 --> 00:04:43.043
"I want to show you guys what I'm thankful for," Bobby said.

71
00:04:43.044 --> 00:04:50.884
Slowly he showed his five things . . . Izzie, Nina, Ethan, Jason, and Miss Shelly.

72
00:04:50.885 --> 00:04:55.287
"Thank you, Bobby!" his friends said.
